// @test regression/INV165-overload-required-param-collision
// @description TV's CE10111: two user-function overloads whose REQUIRED parameter lists match are illegal however many OPTIONAL parameters either one adds, because an optional parameter cannot disambiguate a call that omits it. The arity comparison in INV091's same-arity check cannot see this: `f(float x)` / `f(float x, float scale = 1.0)` collide at different arities, and `g(float x, int s = 1)` / `g(float x, float t = 2.0)` collide at the SAME arity even though the full parameter lists differ. The silent halves carry the rule's false-positive story and are all TV-probed clean (INV165 p1/p2/p4/p5/p8/p10/p11): an UNTYPED required parameter is undetermined and collides with nothing, distinct required types are a legal overload, a differing required ARITY is a legal overload, and a qualifier difference (simple int vs series int) counts as a distinct type. Every line here was diffed against `pine-lint --tv` at zero disagreement, positions and wording included. See INV165, TODO #71.
// @expects parse: success
// @expects errors: 3
// @expects error: line=6, message=/The "collideAcrossArity" function has overloads with the same required parameters/
// @expects error: line=11, message=/The "collideSameArity" function has overloads with the same required parameters/
// @expects error: line=16, message=/The "collideNoRequired" function has overloads with the same required parameters/
//@version=6
indicator("overload required-param collision")

collideAcrossArity(float x) =>
    x + 1.0
collideAcrossArity(float x, float scale = 1.0) =>
    x * scale

collideSameArity(float x, int s = 1) =>
    x * s
collideSameArity(float x, float t = 2.0) =>
    x + t

collideNoRequired() =>
    1.0
collideNoRequired(int s = 1) =>
    s * 2.0

// Legal: distinct required types.
distinctTypes(float x) =>
    x + 1.0
distinctTypes(int x) =>
    x + 1

// Legal: a differing required arity.
distinctArity(float x) =>
    x + 1.0
distinctArity(float x, float y) =>
    x + y

// Legal: an untyped required parameter is undetermined and distinguishes
// nothing, so it collides with nothing - including with an optional-bearing
// sibling.
undetermined(x) =>
    x + 1.0
undetermined(float y, float s = 2.0) =>
    y * s

// Legal: the qualifier is part of the type.
qualifierDistinct(simple int x, int pad = 0) =>
    x + pad
qualifierDistinct(series int x) =>
    x + 2

plot(collideAcrossArity(1.0) + collideSameArity(1.0) + collideNoRequired())
plot(distinctTypes(1.0) + distinctArity(1.0) + undetermined(1.0))
plot(qualifierDistinct(2))
